- Critical: In buy(), token_amount = (swapValue * _balances[address(this)]) / (address(this).balance). If address(this).balance == 0, division by zero. But buy requires tradingEnable. tradingEnable can be set true by addLiquidity which requires msg.value > 0, so balance > 0. But owner can enableTrading(true) before addLiquidity? enableTrading is onlyOwner and can set true at any time. If owner sets tradingEnable = true before any ETH in contract, then receive() calls buy(), address(this).balance = 0, division by zero -> revert. Not catastrophic. But also if removeLiquidity sends all ETH out and sets tradingEnable = false, so safe. Owner could disable trading? Actually enableTrading(false) then true? If removeLiquidity, balance 0, tradingEnable false. Owner can later enableTrading(true) (if owner not renounced) even with balance 0 and liquidityAdded true? Then buy() div by zero. But owner could also send ETH? receive() would call buy() and div by zero if balance 0? Actually if balance 0, receive() calls buy() which computes swapValue = msg.value. If msg.value > 0, address(this).balance is still 0 at that moment? Wait in receive(), msg.value is added to contract balance before function executes? Yes, when receive() is called, the ETH is already transferred to the contract, so address(this).balance includes msg.value. So if someone sends ETH to contract with tradingEnable true and balance was 0, then address(this).balance = msg.value > 0. So no div by zero. In buy(), address(this).balance includes msg.value. So if msg.value > 0, balance > 0. If msg.value == 0, swapValue = 0, token_amount = 0, require token_amount > 0 fails. So no div by zero. But if someone calls transfer to contract (sell) with tradingEnable true and balance 0? sell() computes ethAmount = sell_amount * address(this).balance / (_balances[address(this)] + sell_amount). If balance 0, ethAmount = 0, require ethAmount > 0 fails. So safe. However getAmountOut with reserveETH = 0 and _buy = true: (value * reserveToken) / (0 + value) / 2. If value > 0, ok. If value = 0, division by zero? value + reserveETH = 0, division by zero. But view, not state.

